desc: Copy Cat Pitch Tracker (mda Tracker port) by chmaha
tags: pitch tracker oscillator ring-modulator eq
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Follows the pitch of the input with a sine, square or saw oscillator, a ring modulator, or a peaking EQ
  that tunes itself to the note being played. Tracking works on monophonic sources; on drums, noise and other
  unpitched material it makes strange, evolving pitch sequences. Glide sets how fast the pitch may change,
  Transpose shifts it for harmonics or octave doubling, Maximum rejects tracking errors above a set pitch and
  Trigger stops the tracker in gaps. Dynamics puts the dynamics of the input on the generated sound.
  Ported from mda Tracker by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio), via mda-effects
  https://github.com/pluginguru/mda-effects (MIT or GPLv2+)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
